From a849d8c2047b224de90974b2ab68e5c5c794d75f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:32:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build the OptiX sub-devices of one acceleration structure in
 parallel

MultiDevice::build_bvh built every acceleration structure on one
sub-device after the other: for a large curve geometry or the scene
level structure of a heavily instanced scene the second GPU only started
when the first had finished.

For the MULTI_OPTIX layout the sub-devices of a top level structure and
of a geometry with at least 65,536 primitives now build at the same time on
an isolated parallel loop. Smaller geometries already build in parallel
with each other and keep the sequential loop: a parallel loop per small
geometry cost more than it saved with 20,000 objects. Each uses only its own device, memory and build
lock; the shared curve build input is still computed once, by whichever
sub-device locks it first, under its own mutex. The sequential loop swapped
every geometry's BVH pointer to the sub-device BVH so that a top level build
found its device's bottom level structures through it. The parallel path
leaves the geometry pointers alone and sets the sub-device index on the
sub-device BVH instead; the OptiX top level build uses it to pick the bottom
level structure of its own device from the geometry's multi-device BVH.
Other layouts keep the sequential loop with the pointer swap unchanged. The
environment variable CYCLES_OPTIX_SERIAL_SUBDEVICE_BVH builds one
sub-device after the other as before, as a reference.

Rationale: Sub-devices of one multi-device build are independent, so building them one after the other only added the second device's time to every large or scene level build.
Contract: Every sub-device builds from the same inputs with the same calls as before and a top level build references the same bottom level structures; other layouts and the reference switch keep the sequential loop with the geometry pointer swap.
Tests: tests/houdini_curve_subdivisions_smoke.py
---
 src/bvh/bvh.h                    |  4 ++
 src/device/multi/device.cpp      | 87 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/device/optix/device_impl.cpp | 22 +++++++-
 3 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/bvh/bvh.h b/src/bvh/bvh.h
index 60b1d704ab53e3872a753c6f318f364aacc94049..43583074d106c05abba1d401ac3bf31485f60010 100644
--- a/src/bvh/bvh.h
+++ b/src/bvh/bvh.h
@@ -89,6 +89,10 @@ class BVH {
   /* Non-owning; set only while MultiDevice::build_bvh builds this sub-device BVH. Devices that
    * do not share build data ignore it. */
   BVHSharedBuild *shared_build = nullptr;
+  /* Index of this sub-device BVH in its BVHMulti while MultiDevice::build_bvh builds the
+   * sub-devices in parallel, -1 otherwise. A top level build then finds the bottom level
+   * structures of its own device through the geometry's BVHMulti instead of a swapped pointer. */
+  int multi_sub_index = -1;
 
   static unique_ptr<BVH> create(const BVHParams &params,
                                 const vector<Geometry *> &geometry,
